  "description": "Synopsis with 25 source-matched history records: progress variants, recorded dates/levels, both worlds, long and short texts, page bounds and list scrolling.",
  "registration": "A controlled Rust inventory-fixture changes only 25 scenario records in both copies, with matching progress values, saved levels and UTC timestamps including leap day. Live story stays 2500, party and skit history are unchanged, and the original DTM prefix is retained. This tests menu history presentation, not story progression. Native update 64 registers observed school-grounds ambient origins once. Menu entry is native 76/source VI 12; subsequent input and captures use native update = source VI + 64. There are no loading stalls or later phase adjustments. Synopsis gates compare the complete recorded history, eligible list, selected row and reading mode; party and field effects remain checked. Native page keys match the original C-stick vertically. Source page-up from the final long-text page takes two VIs: VI 1611 starts the operation, VI 1612 presents it without another effect update. Omit that one computation wait thereafter (native = source VI + 63), retaining source-observed effect/RNG checks. The source has no presentation at VI 1791, so the settled return uses VI 1792 on both timelines. Consecutive captures check scrolling and reading-panel fades, including ignored input during both. Source scroll counters advance after drawing; the gate maps native visible poses to that observation. Reopening Synopsis within the main menu retains the selected entry and list page; second and final pages are checked separately. The Main/Synopsis handoff now has consecutive image and fade-state gates in both directions, including ignored transition input; the shaded field copy remains opaque between menu pages. The omitted source VI still advanced the UI clock: add that single UI tick at native update 1675 without advancing gameplay, effects, scripts or random state. UI clock and effect clock have independent state gates, preserving cursor-trail history through later menu transitions.",
